            <ArticleTitle>Bis(N-heterocyclic olefin) Derivative: An Efficient Precursor for Isophosphindolylium Species.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8608-8614</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.inorgchem.6b02991</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have developed bis(N-heterocyclic olefin) derivatives 2 and demonstrated that 2 can be utilized as precursors for the synthesis of isophosphindolylium species 3. X-ray diffraction and density functional theory studies indicate the aromatic property of the PC4 five-membered ring in 3. Despite its cationic nature, the P center in 3b exhibits nucleophilic character and thus readily forms a bond with CuCl to afford a copper phosphenium complex 4, demonstrating the potential utility of 3 as a σ-donor ligand.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
